# Android Compose Design System

- Prefer existing components in `com.youtube.rating.android.ui.components`.
- Do not duplicate top bars, loading states, empty states, rating selectors, media thumbnails, or scaffold behavior without checking existing components first.
- Screen composables render immutable state and forward actions. Business decisions belong in ViewModels/use cases.
- Keep feature UI package-local unless another feature needs a stable public component.
- Use theme tokens from the app theme instead of hardcoded colors for reusable UI.
- Interactive icons and media controls need content descriptions unless they are explicitly decorative.
- Lazy lists should use stable keys when item IDs exist.
- Avoid nested card-heavy layouts for dense app screens; prefer clear sections and reusable rows/cards only for repeated items.
- Text must fit on small screens. Prefer responsive layout constraints over viewport-scaled font sizes.

